"Ben UFO": "Ben UFO is a British electronic music producer and DJ known for his work in the techno and house scenes. He is based in London and has a strong presence in the UK and European electronic music circuits.\nPerforms as: Ben UFO\nTheir channels, stations, shows, clubs, labels, collaborators: Rinse FM; Boiler Room; The Lot Radio; Sub FM; Horst; Dekmantel Festival; Hessle Audio; Kiosk Radio\nOther people with the name (not this artist): Ben UFO (musician) - Based in London, known for techno and house music.; Ben UFO (actor) - An American actor, known for his work in film and television.",
"Daniel Bell": "Daniel Bell is an electronic DJ and producer known for his Detroit techno and deep house sounds. He has played in various cities including Berlin, Detroit, and Stuttgart, and is associated with the Detroit techno scene.\nPerforms as: Daniel Bell\nTheir channels, stations, shows, clubs, labels, collaborators: Boiler Room; G (RICE); SilentChaos Music; RTS.FM; The Stillery; Yoyaku Record Store; The Techno Archive; The Vault Radio Show; Ivory Joe From Kokomo; musicisakindofloving; ElectroBassDub3; ReSoluteNYC; As You Like It; Nando; Dave Turov; Andreas W; 5 Universos Records; paxahau; Closer \u239c Lisnyi Prychal; TinMan; M\u00fcllers B\u00fcro; Dj Metalik; Son of a Stranger (t-funkshun)\nOther people with the name (not this artist): Daniel Bell (Professor) - A professor at Tsinghua University, known for his work on China's political and economic systems.; Daniel Bell (DJ) - An electronic DJ and producer, known for his Detroit techno and deep house sounds.",
"Fred Everything": "Performs as: Fred Everything",
"Phil Weeks": "Phil Weeks is an electronic DJ and producer known for his deep house and tech house sounds. He primarily performs in cities like Paris, London, and Barcelona, and is associated with labels such as Robsoul Recordings.\nPerforms as: Phil Weeks\nTheir channels, stations, shows, clubs, labels, collaborators: Cercle; Phil Weeks; Mixmag; Riot Producciones; Robsoul Recordings; ADE; Rex Club; Get Underground; H2O Club; Fabric London; Moxy Muzik; RARA; Supervibe; We Love International; Delta Funk; Moulton Music; Rinse FM; db Artists Musique; RIN Italia Network; OTR Musica; On The Reg; LostMyDogRecords; Cadenza; House Gangster TV; Rex Club; Robsoul Party; Robsoul Live; Robsoul's Most Wanted; Robsoul's Survival Series\nOther people with the name (not this artist): Phil Weeks (Producer) - Based in the UK, known for his production work and not primarily a DJ.; Phil Weeks (Musician) - Based in the US, known for his work with bands and not primarily a DJ.",
"Tornado Wallace": "Tornado Wallace is an electronic DJ and producer known for his work in the house and techno scenes. He has performed at various festivals and clubs, primarily in Europe and Australia, and collaborates with artists like Fantastic Man, Jamie Tiller, and David Vunk.\nPerforms as: Tornado Wallace\nTheir channels, stations, shows, clubs, labels, collaborators: Boiler Room; History of House Music; Knot for (\u8033); Fault Radio; Sonder Festival; H\u00d6R BERLIN; Studio Namsan; GALA Festival; Love International Festival; RolloverMILANO; Headstream; Sameheads TV; Seoul Community Radio; Tornado Wallace; Bar Part Time; NOT AN ANIMAL Records; Acid Mike; Cricket; Platforma Wolff; Melbourne Deepcast; NTS 2024-2025; Beats In Space; PUBLIC POSSESSION; Golden Plains; 3RRR; NOISE IN MY HEAD; 1BTN\nOther people with the name (not this artist): Tornado Wallace (electronic music) - known for house and techno music, based in Europe and Australia; Tornado Wallace (cyclone) - a weather phenomenon, not related to the electronic music artist"
